From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 77/77] PC5: the shader compiler's listing in Microsoft's syntax,
 room after a large heap block, and parked files reopened under another number
 (Wine patches 0990, 0991, 0994)

0990: the listing fxc.exe's in-process stand-in (0988) writes is in
Microsoft's assembly syntax, so a game that assembles it again with
D3DXAssembleShader gets its shaders instead of an error for each.

0991: a large heap block gets a page of room before its 64 KiB rounding,
so a game that writes one element past the end of one doesn't fault.

0994: a parked folder or read-only file opened again by name is taken
when its file system numbers it anew, and a failure to open one again is
logged instead of failing without a word.
